  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporters of Anti-Trafficking Initiatives (SATI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute to the counter-trafficking (CT) efforts made in Greece by strengthening the local NGOs&apos; capacity to promote and protect the human rights of victims of trafficking. The latter will be achieved through a two-folded intervention targeting Greek NGOs engaged in CT, consisting of the provision of financial resources to support CT activities and the implementation of streamlined capacity-building activities. In particular, building on the initiative of the United States of America (USA) Ambassador in Greece to engage the business community in the fight against trafficking, IOM will establish a coordination mechanism ensuring that donations made by the Greek businesspeople are allocated to NGOs offering valuable assistance in the identification and protection of victims of trafficking.</narrative>
  </description>
